CO2Fix_3_1

100	# simulation lenght [yr]

comments
{
Example how to simulate grassland. 
Mart-Jan Schelhaas
July 2004

This grassland has an NPP of 9 Mg dry matter per hectare per year, of which 5 Mg abovegroudn and 4 Mg belowground. Grass is simulated as a "tree" with a very small stem and a lot of foliage and roots. Increment in the stem is very small, and mortality high to avoid a build up in the stem biomass. Allocation to roots and foliage is then relatively high to get the required NPP rates.

The file contains two scenarios, one with an unmanaged grassland and one with a managed grassland. In the managed scenario, 60% of the biomass is harvested. Since this applies only to the stem compartment, the SlashFirewood box needs to be set at 1, to indicate that all the slash (=foliage) is removed from the site.
}

2	# number of Scenarios

0	# mitigation scenario
0	# baseline scenario

0	# Project duration
0	 #Year of first verification

0	# Base year (or start of crediting period)

0	# NetNet year, year in which base emissions or removals are measured

1	# No Baseline
1	# Exclude products
1	# Exclude bioenergy
0	# Mitigation method (i.e. JI, CDM etc....)
1	# Assist 1 result
0	# Assist 2 result
7	# Carbon selected for comparison between baseline and mitigation scenario (i.e. biomass, soil, total etc..)
-1	# answer0
-1	# answer1
-1	# answer2
-1	# answer3
-1	# answer4
-1	# answer5
-1	# answer6
-1	# answer7
-1	# answer8
-1	# answer9
-1	# answer10
-1	# answer11
-1	# answer12
-1	# answer13
